@startuml
title FoodBridge FB-OCI-CD-001 v1.2.0 — CI, preflight e CD Oracle
actor "Mantenedor" as Maintainer
participant "GitHub Actions" as GH
database "PostgreSQL 16 CI descartável" as CIPG
collections "JAR aprovado / Artifact" as Artifact
participant "SSH (host key fixada)" as SSH
participant "Oracle Linux 9 / opc" as VM
participant "systemd foodbridge.service" as Service
database "PostgreSQL local existente" as ProdPG

Maintainer -> GH : pull_request / push / workflow_dispatch
GH -> CIPG : Iniciar DB efêmero
GH -> GH : Java 21, Gradle test, bootJar, bash -n, unittest
CIPG --> GH : testes concluídos
alt CI falha
  GH --> Maintainer : FAIL, sem SSH
else CI aprova
  GH -> Artifact : Upload JAR aprovado
  alt preflight=true, deploy=false, main
    GH -> SSH : Login dedicado + known_hosts verificado
    SSH -> VM : bash -s verificar-vm.sh (leitura)
    VM -> Service : consultar User/ExecStart/Environment/health
    VM --> GH : PASS / FAIL sem alterar VM
  else deploy=true, OCI_DEPLOY_ENABLED=true
    GH -> SSH : Preflight obrigatório primeiro
    SSH -> VM : Verificar service, Jar, config, ddl-auto, saúde
    alt preflight não aprova
      VM --> GH : FAIL; nada substituído
    else preflight aprova
      GH -> SSH : SCP artifact aprovado; SHA-256
      SSH -> VM : atualizar-api.sh
      VM -> VM : backup JAR antigo / troca atômica
      VM -> Service : restart e health local
      alt health falha
        VM -> VM : restaurar JAR anterior
        VM -> Service : restart / health do rollback
        VM --> GH : FAIL, rollback reportado
      else health OK
        VM --> GH : DEPLOY OK
      end
    end
  else push, auto não habilitado
    GH --> Maintainer : deploy-oracle SKIPPED
  end
end
note over VM,ProdPG
Os scripts do CI/CD não executam SQL, mas o reinício
do Spring exige revisão do ddl-auto e de migrações.
Nenhum teste de CI usa o PostgreSQL existente.
end note
@enduml
